      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Given your new hyperthyroidism diagnosis and existing ADHD treatment, your racing heart and jitteriness are likely a sign of medication interaction that requires immediate attention from your doctors. You should **not** adjust your Adderall or thyroid medication independently, as both stimulants and thyroid hormones significantly impact heart rate. Please contact your primary care physician or endocrinologist promptly to discuss potential dosage reductions or alternative therapies to ensure both your focus needs and thyroid health remain stable.",
