      "content": "Cutting your dose in half without medical supervision is dangerous because it provides immediate relief only to create a sudden rebound effect on your heart rate when you restart your full dose, potentially worsening your anxiety and thyroid symptoms. Doing this while experiencing new hyperthyroidism signs could lead to dangerous heart arrhythmias that far exceed the risks of temporary overstimulation. Given your project deadline, your doctor may have other short-term solutions like switching to a different ADHD medication that interacts less aggressively with your thyroid condition than Adderall. Please reach out to your doctor's office again today specifically requesting an emergency bridge plan for your work until the three-week appointment arrives.",
